Newspeak3
'Test'
(* A nested class's superclass clause that names a predefined class finds a
   member of that name an enclosing class declares. newspeak-spec.pdf 6.1
   evaluates the clause `String new` "as if it occurred inside an instance
   method" of the enclosing class, so its `String` is an implicit receiver
   send, and 5.7 answers it with the innermost lexically enclosing
   declaration: the module's nested class `String`, i.e. `outer
   EnclosingBuiltinName String`. `Object`'s accessor for the predefined
   class (3.2) is reached only "if no lexically visible matching method is
   found" (2.3.1), which is not the case here, so `Derived` inherits `tag`.

   The member is a class named `String` rather than one named `Object`: a
   nested class `Object = Object new` finds itself in its own clause by the
   same rule and is refused as a cyclic class definition. *)
class EnclosingBuiltinName = Object new () (
    class String = Object new () (
        public tag = ( ^'local' )
    )
    class Derived = String new () ()
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        platform transcript show: Derived new tag; newLine
    )
) : ()
